27. Amendment and repeal of Statutes and Regulations'- The procedure foradding to, amending or repealing the Statutes and the Regulations shall be the sameas that prescribed respectively for framing or making Statutes and Regulations'
28. Rules.-(1) The Authorities and the other bodies of the University may make Rules' to bepublishedintheof-ficialGazette,consistentwiththeOrdinance'StatutescrtheRegulations,toregulateanymatterrelatingtotheaffairsoftheUniversitywhich has not been provided for by the Ordinance or thaf is not required to beregulated by Statutes or Regulations' including rules to regulate the conductof business and the time and place of meetings and related matters'(2) Rules sha1l become effective upon approval by the Board'
(1)
CHAPTERVIGENERAL PROVISIONS26. Indemnity and bar of jurisdiction'-No suit, prosecution or other legal proceeding shall lie against any person orauthority for an)'thing which is in good faith done or intended to be done un<ler
this Bill.
(2) No decision taken, or act or thing done' by the Chancellor or the Board shallbe called in question before any Court or other authority'21 . Bill to override other laws'- This Bill shall have efi'ectnotwithstanding anythrng contained in any other law for the time being in force'28. Removal of difficulties'-(l) If any question arises as to the interpretation of any of the provisions of thisBill,itshallbeplacedbeforetheChanceliorwhosedecisionthereonshallbe
final.
