(iv) Where the Board does not. within the time specified, act to thesatisfaction of the Chancellor, the Chancellor may issue suchdirections as the Chancellor considers fit and the Board shall comply' with all such directions.12. Pro-Chancellor.-(l) The Pro-Chancellor shall be appointed by the Chancellor for such period andon such terms as the Chancellor may determine.(2) At any time when the office of Chancellor is vacant, or the Chancellor isabsent or cannot perform the functions ofhis office due to any cause, the Pro-Chancellor shall act for him.(3) The Pro-Chancellor shall perform such other functions as entrusted to him bythe Chancellor.13. Vice Chancellor.-(l) The Vice Chancellor, who shall be an eminent academic or a distinguishedadministrator, sha1l be appointed by the Chancellor, for such period and onsuch terms and conditions, as the Chancellor may determine.(2) The Vice-Chancellor shall be the chief academic and administrative officer ofthe University and shall have overall responsibility for the direction,organization, administration and programmes of the University' under theguidelines and general policies formulated by the Board, and forimplementing the decisions and policies of the Board.(3) Subject to approval of the Chancellor, the Vice Chancellor may delegate suchof his powers and functions under this Bill to such person as he maydetermine, including but not limited to, the academic and administrativeaffairs of the university. Every such person shall report and be responsible tothe Vice Chancellor, who shall be responsible to the Chancellor.
